  "properties": {
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Raffle Entry Manager</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  <script src=\"script.js\" defer></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n  <header>\n    <h1>Raffle Admin Dashboard</h1>\n  </header>\n\n  <main>\n    <div id=\"controls\">\n      <button id=\"showAllBtn\" class=\"secondary-btn\">Show All Entries</button>\n      <button id=\"showTopBtn\" class=\"primary-btn\">Filter Top Candidates</button>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"statusMessage\">Showing: All Entries</div>\n\n    <ul id=\"entriesList\"></ul>\n  </main>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
          "active": true,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "// 1. DOM Elements\nconst entriesList = document.querySelector(\"#entriesList\");\nconst showAllBtn = document.querySelector(\"#showAllBtn\");\nconst showTopBtn = document.querySelector(\"#showTopBtn\");\nconst statusMessage = document.querySelector(\"#statusMessage\");\n\n// 2. Data\nconst raffleEntries = [\n  { id: 1, name: \"Aisha Khan\", email: \"aisha.k@mail.com\", age: 28, reason: \"I am a huge fan of the organizer's mission and want to support it! Very excited for this chance.\", distance_km: 4.5, referralSource: \"Email Newsletter\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 2, name: \"Bot1748\", email: \"bot_entry@placeholder.com\", age: null, reason: \"WINNING IS THE BEST. I REQUIRE ENTRY NOW. WINNING IS THE BEST. I REQUIRE ENTRY NOW.\", distance_km: null, referralSource: \"Social Media Ad\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 3, name: \"John Smith\", email: \"jsmith@generic.net\", age: 41, reason: \"Don't know.\", distance_km: 150, referralSource: \"Search Engine\", uniqueEntry: false },\n  { id: 4, name: \"Marie Dubois\", email: \"dubois_m@email.fr\", age: 33, reason: \"I've followed this event for years and finally have the chance to participate. I live close by!\", distance_km: 1.2, referralSource: \"Referral Code\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 5, name: \"Priya Sharma\", email: \"p.sharma@domain.co\", age: \"Prefer not to say\", reason: \"No reason.\", distance_km: 8.9, referralSource: \"Social Media Ad\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 6, name: \"Alex\", email: \"alex123@web.com\", age: 22, reason: \"I need to win the prize for my sister's birthday gift.\", distance_km: 7.0, referralSource: \"Email Newsletter\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 7, name: \"Zoe Chen\", email: \"zchen@test.com\", age: 18, reason: \"...\", distance_km: 50, referralSource: \"Search Engine\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 8, name: \"Omar Hassan\", email: \"omar_h@corp.org\", age: 55, reason: \"I have decades of experience with these types of raffles and believe I am a strong candidate.\", distance_km: 3.1, referralSource: \"Referral Code\", uniqueEntry: false },\n  { id: 9, name: \"Mia Rodriguez\", email: \"mia.r@email.es\", age: 29, reason: \"This is a great opportunity. Looking forward to it!\", distance_km: 9.9, referralSource: \"Social Media Ad\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 10, name: \"Rajesh K.\", email: \"rajeshk@internet.biz\", age: 60, reason: \"I hope to win.\", distance_km: 2500, referralSource: \"Other\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 11, name: \"S. Lee\", email: \"S.Lee@work.net\", age: 35, reason: \"I am available for the event dates and meet all criteria.\", distance_km: 0.5, referralSource: \"Email Newsletter\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 12, name: \"Taehyung Kim\", email: \"taehyung.k@mail.kr\", age: 27, reason: \"My friend told me to enter.\", distance_km: 12.3, referralSource: \"Referral Code\", uniqueEntry: false },\n  { id: 13, name: \"Sarah G.\", email: \"sarahg@mail.com\", age: 38, reason: \"Absolutely love the prizes and would use them responsibly!\", distance_km: 6.1, referralSource: \"Social Media Ad\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 14, name: \"Chris N.\", email: \"chrisn@corp.co\", age: \"N/A\", reason: \"I am interested in winning. The reason is simple: prize.\", distance_km: 20.0, referralSource: \"Search Engine\", uniqueEntry: true },\n  { id: 15, name: \"Eva Mendez\", email: \"eva.m@mail.com\", age: 30, reason: \"This raffle is for a good cause, and I want to support it! Excellent initiative.\", distance_km: 2.8, referralSource: \"Referral Code\", uniqueEntry: true }\n];\n\n// 3. Event Listeners\nshowAllBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  statusMessage.textContent = \"Showing: All Entries\";\n  renderEntries(raffleEntries);\n});\n\nshowTopBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  statusMessage.textContent = \"Showing: Top Candidates Only\";\n  let topList = filterTopCandidates();\n  renderEntries(topList);\n});\n\n// 4. Functions\n\n// ANALYZE THIS: How does the computer decide who is a \"Top Candidate\"?\nfunction filterTopCandidates() {\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n}\n\n\n\n// Render Helper\nfunction renderEntries(list) {\n  entriesList.innerHTML = \"\";\n  \n  if (list.length === 0) {\n    entriesList.innerHTML = \"<li>No entries match this filter.</li>\";\n    return;\n  }\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n    const entry = list[i];\n    const li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n\n    // Visual helpers to spot why someone might fail\n    // If uniqueEntry is false, we make it red (.alert)\n    const uniqueClass = entry.uniqueEntry ? \"good\" : \"alert\";\n    \n    // If age is not a number (like \"N/A\"), highlighting it helps analysis\n    const ageDisplay = (typeof entry.age === 'number') ? entry.age : `<span class=\"alert\">${entry.age}</span>`;\n\n    li.innerHTML = `\n      <h3>${entry.name} <small>(ID: ${entry.id})</small></h3>\n      <span class=\"email\">${entry.email}</span>\n      \n      <div class=\"data-row\">\n        <span>Unique Entry:</span>\n        <span class=\"${uniqueClass}\">${entry.uniqueEntry}</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"data-row\">\n        <span>Age:</span>\n        <span>${ageDisplay}</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"data-row\">\n        <span>Distance:</span>\n        <span>${entry.distance_km} km</span>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"reason-box\">\n        \"${entry.reason}\"\n      </div>\n    `;\n    \n    entriesList.appendChild(li);\n  }\n}\n\n// Initial Render\nrenderEntries(raffleEntries);",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": "/* Base Layout */\nbody {\n  font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n  background-color: #f0f2f5;\n  color: #1c1e21;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 20px;\n}\n\nheader {\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;\n  padding-bottom: 10px;\n}\n\n/* Button Styles */\n#controls {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 15px;\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  padding: 12px 24px;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  border: none;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background 0.2s;\n}\n\n.primary-btn {\n  background-color: #007bff;\n  color: white;\n}\n\n.primary-btn:hover { background-color: #0056b3; }\n\n.secondary-btn {\n  background-color: #6c757d;\n  color: white;\n}\n\n.secondary-btn:hover { background-color: #545b62; }\n\n#statusMessage {\n  font-weight: bold;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n  margin-bottom: 15px;\n  color: #444;\n}\n\n/* Data Cards */\n#entriesList {\n  list-style: none;\n  padding: 0;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));\n  gap: 20px;\n}\n\nli {\n  background: white;\n  padding: 20px;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\n  border-top: 4px solid #007bff;\n}\n\nli h3 {\n  margin-top: 0;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n\n.email {\n  color: #666;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  margin-bottom: 15px;\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.data-row {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n  font-size: 0.95rem;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;\n  padding-bottom: 2px;\n}\n\n.reason-box {\n  background: #f9f9f9;\n  padding: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  margin-top: 10px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n/* Analysis Helpers: Styles to highlight 'bad' data */\n.alert {\n  color: #d9534f; /* Red */\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n\n.good {\n  color: #5cb85c; /* Green */\n  font-weight: bold;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "2",
        "1",
        "3"
      ]
    },
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Do This\r\n\r\nYou are judging an online raffle and there are so many applicants! A quick look at the data shows it is full of bots, duplicate entries, and candidates who don't meet the age requirements.\r\n\r\n**Your Task:** Write the filter logic to clean up the list and identify only the valid, eligible winners.\r\n\r\n1.  **Analyze the Data:** Look at the `raffleEntries` array in `script.js`. Identify the properties that should determine a valid entry.\r\n\r\n2.  **Build the Filter:** Inside the `filterTopCandidates()` function, create filters that select only the top candidates based on the criteria you determine.\r\n\r\n3.  **Test and Refine:** Run the app and click \"Filter Top Candidates.\" Does the final list look like a set of real, eligible humans?\r\n\r\n-----\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Need help? Ask the AI Tutor.</summary>\r\n    <ul>\r\n    <li>How do I check if a boolean property like <code>uniqueEntry</code> is true?</li>\r\n    <li>How do I write an if-statement that checks three different things at once?</li>\r\n    <li>My code isn't filtering out the entries with <code>'Age: null'</code>. How do I fix that?</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n</details>",
